E('eiffel tower', 'The Eiffel Tower is a wrought-iron tower in Paris.', 'It was completed in 1889 for the World’s Fair.', 'It was designed by Gustave Eiffel’s company.', 'It is about 330 metres tall.', 'Many Parisians hated it at first.', 'It was meant to stand for only 20 years but became France’s symbol.', 'It grows several centimetres taller in summer heat.')
E('statue of liberty', 'The Statue of Liberty is a giant copper statue in New York Harbor.', 'It was dedicated on 28 October 1886.', 'It was a gift from France to the United States.', 'It was designed by Frédéric Auguste Bartholdi; Gustave Eiffel built its frame.', 'It turned green as its copper oxidised.', 'It became a symbol of welcome for immigrants.')
E('taj mahal', 'The Taj Mahal is a white marble mausoleum in Agra, India.', 'It was built between about 1632 and 1653.', 'The Mughal emperor Shah Jahan built it for his wife, Mumtaz Mahal.', 'About 20,000 workers built it.', 'Its marble changes colour with the light.', 'It is seen as a masterpiece of Mughal architecture.')
E('stonehenge', 'Stonehenge is a prehistoric stone circle in southern England.', 'It was built in stages from about 3000 to 1500 BC.', 'Some stones came from Wales, about 240 kilometres away.', 'It lines up with the sunrise at the summer solstice.', 'Its purpose is still debated, but it was probably a ceremonial site.', 'It is one of the most famous prehistoric monuments in the world.')
E('parthenon|acropolis', 'The Parthenon is an ancient temple on the Acropolis of Athens.', 'It was built between 447 and 432 BC.', 'It was dedicated to the goddess Athena.', 'It was built under Pericles.', 'It was badly damaged by an explosion in 1687.', 'Some of its sculptures, the Elgin Marbles, are in the British Museum.')
E('petra', 'Petra is an ancient city carved into rock in southern Jordan.', 'It was the capital of the Nabataean kingdom from around the 4th century BC.', 'Its most famous building is the Treasury.', 'It was a major trading hub.', 'It was rediscovered by Europeans in 1812.', 'It is one of the New Seven Wonders of the World.')
E('angkor wat', 'Angkor Wat is a vast temple complex in Cambodia.', 'It was built in the early 12th century.', 'It was built by King Suryavarman II of the Khmer Empire.', 'It was first a Hindu temple, later Buddhist.', 'It is the largest religious monument in the world.', 'It appears on Cambodia’s flag.')
E('seven wonders|seven wonders of the ancient world', 'The Seven Wonders of the Ancient World were famous structures listed by Greek writers.', 'The list dates from around the 2nd century BC.', 'They were the Great Pyramid, the Hanging Gardens of Babylon, the Statue of Zeus at Olympia, the Temple of Artemis, the Mausoleum at Halicarnassus, the Colossus of Rhodes and the Lighthouse of Alexandria.', 'Only the Great Pyramid survives.', 'The Hanging Gardens may never have existed.')
E('library of alexandria', 'The Library of Alexandria was one of the largest libraries of the ancient world.', 'It was founded in the 3rd century BC in Egypt.', 'It may have held hundreds of thousands of scrolls.', 'Scholars there measured the Earth’s size and edited Homer.', 'It declined gradually, rather than in one great fire.', 'It is a symbol of lost knowledge.')
E('notre dame|notre-dame', 'Notre-Dame de Paris is a medieval Gothic cathedral in Paris.', 'Construction began in 1163 and was mostly finished by 1260.', 'It is famous for its flying buttresses and rose windows.', 'Victor Hugo’s The Hunchback of Notre-Dame made it famous.', 'A fire destroyed its spire and roof in April 2019.', 'It reopened in December 2024 after restoration.')
E('big ben', 'Big Ben is the nickname of the great bell in the clock tower of the Palace of Westminster in London.', 'The bell was cast in 1858, and the clock started in 1859.', 'The tower was renamed the Elizabeth Tower in 2012.', 'The bell weighs over 13 tonnes.', 'It is one of London’s most famous landmarks.')
E('kremlin', 'The Kremlin is a fortified complex in the centre of Moscow.', 'Its current walls date from the late 15th century.', 'It is the official residence of the Russian president.', 'It contains palaces and cathedrals.', 'It stands beside Red Square and St Basil’s Cathedral.')
E('machu picchu ruins|lost city of the incas', 'Machu Picchu is a 15th-century Inca citadel high in the Andes of Peru.', 'It was built around 1450.', 'It was abandoned about a century later.', 'Hiram Bingham brought it to world attention in 1911.', 'It sits about 2,430 metres above sea level.', 'It is one of the New Seven Wonders of the World.')
E('mount everest|everest|edmund hillary|tenzing norgay', 'Mount Everest is the highest mountain on Earth.', 'Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay first reached the summit on 29 May 1953.', 'It stands about 8,849 metres above sea level.', 'It sits on the border of Nepal and China.', 'In Nepal it is called Sagarmatha.', 'Hundreds of people now climb it each year.')
E('golden gate bridge', 'The Golden Gate Bridge is a suspension bridge in San Francisco.', 'It opened in 1937.', 'It spans the strait between San Francisco Bay and the Pacific.', 'Its colour is called “International Orange”.', 'It was the longest suspension bridge in the world when it opened.')
E('mount rushmore', 'Mount Rushmore is a mountain sculpture in South Dakota.', 'It was carved between 1927 and 1941.', 'It shows Washington, Jefferson, Theodore Roosevelt and Lincoln.', 'Each face is about 18 metres tall.', 'The land is sacred to the Lakota Sioux.')
E('sydney opera house', 'The Sydney Opera House is a performing arts centre in Australia.', 'It opened in 1973.', 'It was designed by Danish architect Jørn Utzon.', 'Its roof looks like sails.', 'It is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.')
E('christ the redeemer', 'Christ the Redeemer is a giant statue of Jesus overlooking Rio de Janeiro.', 'It was completed in 1931.', 'It stands 30 metres tall, not counting its base.', 'It is made of reinforced concrete and soapstone.', 'It is one of the New Seven Wonders of the World.')
